00:44:00,000 --> 00:44:06,000
Hansel & Gretel: Witch Hunters is a 2013 American fantasy film starring Jeremy Renner and Gemma Arterton as the siblings from
the fairy tale "Hansel and Gretel", who are now grown up and work together to exterminate witches for hire.

13
00:47:40,000 --> 00:47:46,000
The supporting cast includes Famke Janssen and Peter Stormare.

14
00:51:20,000 --> 00:51:26,000
It was written and directed by Tommy Wirkola.

15
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:06,000
In late 2010, after being approached by Gary Sanchez Productions,
Wirkola pitched the film to Paramount Pictures.

16
00:58:40,000 --> 00:58:46,000
Renner was cast as Hansel in September 2010 whilst the role of Gretel was
planned for Noomi Rapace before Arterton's casting in January 2011.

17
01:02:20,000 --> 01:02:26,000
Principal photography began in March 2011 at Babelsberg
Studio in Germany, and concluded in June.

18
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
Originally scheduled for release in March 2012, the film was delayed to allow
additional time to shoot a post-credits scene with Renner.

19
01:09:40,000 --> 01:09:46,000
Hansel and Gretel: Witch Hunters was theatrically released
in the United States on January 25, 2013.

20
01:13:20,000 --> 01:13:26,000
It received generally negative reviews from critics for
its weak script and gratuitous violence.

21
01:17:00,000 --> 01:17:06,000
It was a box-office success, grossing $226 million
against a production budget of $50 million.

22
01:20:40,000 --> 01:20:46,000
The film explores themes of witch, gun, witch burning, black magic, troll.

23
01:24:20,000 --> 01:24:26,000
The tone is dark.
